      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Do not use superglue on a deep puncture, as it traps bacteria and debris inside the wound, which can lead to a severe, life-threatening infection known as an abscess or osteomyelitis. Hydrogen peroxide damages healthy tissue and is ineffective at penetrating deep wounds to clean them properly, making it a poor choice for this injury. Since puncture wounds are high-risk for infection regardless of tetanus status, please see a medical professional immediately to get professional irrigation and a proper antiseptic tissue seal before working. Your safety is far more important than finishing the landscaping project this week.",
