      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While I cannot offer medical advice, avoiding a doctor's visit for a deep rust puncture carries a serious risk, especially given your financial constraints. Soaking the wound in warm salt water may help gently clean the surface, but it will not remove debris trapped deep inside or provide the sterile environment needed to prevent infection from soil bacteria. Instead of trying to \"seal\" it with ointment or bandages immediately, the safest temporary measure while you explore low-cost options like visiting a free clinic or community health center is to clean it gently with soap and water and elevate your foot to reduce swelling. Please consider contacting your local hospital or public health department to discuss financial assistance programs, as delaying treatment could result in costly complications down the road.",
